eudev is the standalone udev: udevd, udevadm and the stock rules. It creates device
permissions (input, audio, video groups), handles hotplug and coldplug at boot through
03-udev.sh in /etc/rc.d/boot, and provides the real libudev. It replaces libudev-zero:
it installs libudev.so.1 over it, which libinput and wlroots keep using without a rebuild.
Built without manpages, blkid, kmod, selinux and mtd support, with the hwdb enabled.
Rules: /usr/local/lib/udev/rules.d, your own rules: /etc/udev/rules.d.
